ec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and valid next states\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: validation error\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates which field/value failed validation\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: error in JSON mode\n    When: --json is active\n    Then: guidance included in structured error object\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-dry-run ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: command supports dry run\n    When: --dry-run flag is provided\n    Then: show what would be changed without applying\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: command completes\n    Then: no files are modified\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: output is shown\n    Then: clear indication that this is a preview\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: command would error\n    Then: error shown but no state changed\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: --dry-run and --force both provided\n    When: command executes\n    Then: dry run takes precedence (no changes made)\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run in JSON mode\n    When: --dry-run --json provided\n    Then: JSON output includes dry_run boolean field\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-shadow-commit ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command modifies state in shadow worktree\n    When: save operation completes successfully\n    Then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: commit message is generated\n    Then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":9253574},"formatted_output":"kspec batch --commands '' hangs instead of erroring — empty/missing args should fail fast with a cle\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJDQ18VNYYAXETR8WREAJW2X\nType:      task\nStatus:    pending\nPriority:  3\nAutomation: eligible\n\n─── Description ───\n  **What**: `kspec batch --commands ''` hangs instead of failing fast. When Commander receives `--commands ''` (empty string), `options.commands` is `''` which is falsy in JavaScript. The source selection logic at `src/cli/commands/batch.ts` line 148 (`else if (options.commands)`) skips the inline path and falls through to `source = { type: 'stdin' }`. The stdin reader at `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 114-124 then blocks forever waiting for input that will never come.\n  \n  **Where**:\n  - `src/cli/commands/batch.ts` lines 146-152 — source selection logic\n  - `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 100-126 — `readSource()` stdin path\n  \n  **How**:\n  Change the source selection to check `options.commands !== undefined` instead of truthiness:\n  ```typescript\n  if (options.file) {\n    source = { type: 'file', path: options.file };\n  } else if (options.commands !== undefined) {\n    source = { type: 'inline', json: options.commands };\n  } else {\n    source = { type: 'stdin' };\n  }\n  ```\n  This way `--commands ''` takes the inline path and gets caught by `parseBatchInput()` which will fail on `JSON.parse('')` with a clear 'Invalid JSON' error.\n  \n  Alternatively, also add early validation in the inline path: if `options.commands` is empty/whitespace, throw `BatchParseError('Empty --commands value')` before attempting parse.\n  \n  **Done when**:\n  - `kspec batch --commands ''` exits immediately with a clear error (not a hang)\n  - `kspec batch --commands ' '` also fails fast\n  - No regression: `kspec batch --commands '[...]'` still works correctly\n  - Add a test case for empty `--commands` input\nSpec ref:  @batch-exec\nCreated:   2026-02-26T19:32:56.309Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nBatch Command Execution\nType: feature\nImplementation: in_progress\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-stdin]\n    Given: JSON array piped via stdin\n    When: kspec batch runs with no --file or --commands flag\n    Then: Commands are read from stdin and executed in order\n  [ac-file]\n    Given: --file flag with path to JSON file\n    When: kspec batch --file commands.json runs\n    Then: Commands are read from the file and executed in order\n  [ac-inline]\n    Given: --commands flag with JSON string\n    When: kspec batch --commands with inline JSON runs\n    Then: Inline JSON is parsed and commands execute\n  [ac-stop-on-error]\n    Given: Default mode (no --continue flag) with 5 commands where command 3 fails at runtime\n    When: Batch executes\n    Then: In atomic mode: all changes rolled back. In immediate mode: commands 1-2 committed, commands 4-5 not executed. Exit code is 1\n  [ac-continue]\n    Given: Immediate mode (--continue implies --no-atomic) with 5 commands where command 3 fails at runtime\n    When: Batch executes\n    Then: All 5 commands are attempted, command 3 failure is recorded, other commands succeed, exit code is 1\n  [ac-prevalidate]\n    Given: Batch with 3 commands where command 2 has invalid syntax\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Validation fails before any execution, no commands run, error identifies the invalid command by index, exit code is 1\n  [ac-dry-run]\n    Given: --dry-run flag with valid batch\n    When: kspec batch --dry-run runs\n    Then: All commands are validated but not executed, output shows what would run, no state changes occur\n  [ac-forward-ref]\n    Given: Batch where command 2 references slug created by command 1\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Pre-validation recognizes the forward reference as valid, execution succeeds for both commands\n  [ac-single-commit]\n    Given: Atomic mode (default) with 3 successful mutating commands\n    When: Batch completes successfully\n    Then: A single shadow branch commit is created containing all changes (not 3 separate commits)\n  [ac-partial-commit]\n    Given: Immediate mode with --continue, commands 1-2 succeed, command 3 fails\n    When: Batch completes with partial success\n    Then: 2 individual commits (commands 1-2), no commit for command 3\n  [ac-mutating-only]\n    Given: Batch containing a read-only command like item get\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Validation rejects with error identifying the non-mutating command\n  [ac-confirmation-suppressed]\n    Given: Batch containing a command that normally requires confirmation (e.g., item delete without --force)\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Command executes without prompting for confirmation (batch mode is implicitly non-interactive)\n  [ac-invalid-json]\n    Given: Malformed JSON input (from any source)\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Parse error with line/position info if available, exit code 1, no commands executed\n  [ac-empty-batch]\n    Given: Empty JSON array []\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Error message says batch contains no commands, exit code 1\n  [ac-default-atomic]\n    Given: kspec batch runs without --no-atomic\n    When: Batch executes\n    Then: Atomic mode: commands execute against isolated copy of state\n  [ac-atomic-rollback]\n    Given: Atomic mode, 5 cmds where cmd 3 fails\n    When: Batch encounters failure\n    Then: ALL changes discarded, no shadow commit, state identical to before batch, exit 1\n  [ac-atomic-isolation]\n    Given: Atomic mode, commands modifying state\n    When: Batch is executing\n    Then: Modifications in isolated copy; other kspec operations see original state\n  [ac-no-atomic-flag]\n    Given: --no-atomic flag provided\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Immediate mode: per-command commits, no rollback\n  [ac-immediate-per-commit]\n    Given: Immediate mode, 3 successful commands\n    When: Batch completes\n    Then: 3 individual shadow commits (one per command)\n  [ac-immediate-no-rollback]\n    Given: Immediate mode, 5 cmds where cmd 3 fails\n    When: Batch stops\n    Then: Commands 1-2 remain committed, cmds 4-5 not executed, exit 1\n  [ac-continue-implies-immediate]\n    Given: --continue without --no-atomic\n    When: kspec batch runs\n    Then: Immediate mode activated implicitly with notice in output\n  [ac-json-mode-field]\n    Given: --json flag provided\n    When: Batch completes\n    Then: JSON output includes mode field: atomic or immediate\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-json-output ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports JSON mode\n    When: --json flag is provided\n    Then: output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command completes successfully\n    Then: output includes all data available in human-readable mode\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command encounters an error\n    Then: error is returned as JSON object with error field\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains references\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: references use @ prefix consistently\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains timestamps\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: timestamps use ISO 8601 format\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports --json\n    When: used with other formatting flags\n    Then: --json takes precedence over other format options\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-semantic-exit-codes ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: command completes successfully\n    When: operation succeeds\n    Then: exit code 0\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: command encounters validation error\n    When: user input is invalid\n    Then: exit code 1\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: command is cancelled by user\n    When: confirmation prompt declined\n    Then: exit code 2\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: command encounters runtime error\n    When: operation fails during execution\n    Then: exit code 3\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: command finds nothing\n    When: query returns no results\n    Then: exit code 0 with empty result set\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: command used incorrectly\n    When: invalid flags or arguments provided\n    Then: exit code 1 with usage information\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: batch operation completes\n    When: partial failures occur\n    Then: exit code 1\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-semantic-exit-codes)\n    Given: command documentation\n    When: developers implement commands\n    Then: exit code meanings documented in code\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-error-guidance ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes description of what went wrong\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes suggested action to resolve\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: reference not found\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and valid next states\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: validation error\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates which field/value failed validation\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: error in JSON mode\n    When: --json is active\n    Then: guidance included in structured error object\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-dry-run ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: command supports dry run\n    When: --dry-run flag is provided\n    Then: show what would be changed without applying\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: command completes\n    Then: no files are modified\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: output is shown\n    Then: clear indication that this is a preview\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: command would error\n    Then: error shown but no state changed\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: --dry-run and --force both provided\n    When: command executes\n    Then: dry run takes precedence (no changes made)\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run in JSON mode\n    When: --dry-run --json provided\n    Then: JSON output includes dry_run boolean field\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-shadow-commit ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command modifies state in shadow worktree\n    When: save operation completes successfully\n    Then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: commit message is generated\n    Then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n","status":"completed"}